Vita: process J3D's display lists in place, and know the arrays they load (port of
the 3DS port's Aurora patches 0004 and 0006).

GXCallDisplayList copies a display list into the FIFO every call, because the caller may change or
free it afterwards. GXCallDisplayListStatic queues a reference (address, size, id) instead; the
command processor processes the list where it is and tells the Vita backend which list it is in
(twv_gfx_static_dl) and which list every array base came from (twv_gfx_array_base, also from the
fast decoder of patch 0003). The id changes with GXInvalidateDisplayListStatic, which the caller
calls after every change to a list's bytes (patches/dusklight/0014 does for J3D);
GXInvalidateArrayStatic names arrays their owner changes in place (twv_gx_array_dynamic /
twv_gx_array_gen). The mode is chosen at start-up by the backend (twv_gx_static_dl_mode): 0 copies
every list as upstream does, 1 goes by reference, 2 also hashes each list at the call and at its
processing and reports any change made without an invalidation. Same commands, same order.

